Meanwhile features

The half-tab you sit with while a Cursor agent runs. The column is narrow, so each feature has to earn that space. Ordered by what makes the wait useful first.

Live session





Render .meanwhile/session.json, the file the hooks already write, instead of the static preview.



Remove the Empty / Video / Ask / Both toggles once real session state drives the panel.



Keep the layout from the black stage: centered column, video, one card, corner mark.



Take colors from the IDE theme so the panel belongs in Cursor.

What this wait is





A header in one line: Meanwhile · ~6–10 min · Stripe · Next.js.



Stack chips only for technologies on the allowlist that this task actually touches.



A wait range from a small heuristic (how much work is in front of the agent), updated if the run runs long.



One activity line in plain language (“wiring the checkout route”), refreshed as the agent moves.



Something to watch





One curated video chosen for the stack in the header, with a title and a length.



An “Up next” line: the following clip’s title and length, not a playlist.



A short fallback clip when no YouTube key is configured.



A clip whose length fits the estimate, so a two-minute task does not open a twenty-minute video.



When the estimate was short and the run continues, roll forward to Up next.



One question





A single card when the agent is blocked on a constraint the repo cannot answer. The reference card is “Only you can decide”.



Three short choices. The picked choice is marked, then the card collapses to one line: the constraint you set.



That answer goes back to the agent for the rest of the run.



One open card at a time.



Answer from the keyboard, with the same shortcut that opens the panel.



When the agent stops





The header switches to “Review the diff”.



One sentence on what changed (“Checkout route added, 4 files”), then the column steps aside for the diff.



The video stops with the run.



Quiet by default





The stage stays empty until a video or a question exists.



The corner mark stays.



No points, streaks, or a second list of goals and timers on this surface.

